# Cloudflare serves these on every response. Audit finding 19 added the CSP.
#
# IT IS NOW ENFORCING. It ran as Report-Only from the audit until 2026-08-21.
#
# It was NOT flipped on "Sentry has been quiet", which is weak evidence: Sentry
# only hears about pages real people happened to open in a real browser, so a
# screen nobody visited that week reports nothing and breaks on the day you
# enforce. It was flipped after the policy was tested DIRECTLY -- the real
# production build served locally with this exact policy as an enforcing header,
# every route walked, and every origin named below probed one at a time, with an
# unlisted host as a control to prove the policy was actually blocking.
#
# What that test proved, all with zero violations: images from BOTH
# auth.gosalka.com and the .supabase.co host load; OpenStreetMap tiles load; the
# Google Fonts stylesheet loads via <link>; the Supabase REST API, the FCM and
# Firebase-installations endpoints are reachable; and the realtime WebSocket
# (wss://) OPENS -- while an unlisted image host and an unlisted wss:// host
# were both refused, so enforcement was demonstrably live.
#
# TWO THINGS THE TEST COULD NOT REACH, recorded honestly:
#
#   The staff portals. /admin, /vendor, /driver, /supervisor, /catalog and
#   /observer all redirect to /login without a session, so those screens were
#   never rendered. Their ingredients were each proved separately -- leaflet is
#   bundled and covered by 'self', the tiles load, https and wss to Supabase both
#   work -- but the assembled screens were not exercised.
#
#   The service worker. firebase-messaging-sw.js importScripts the FCM SDK from
#   www.gstatic.com, and script-src lists that host precisely so it may. It could
#   not be executed under test: registration fails in the test browser on
#   localhost, and fails IDENTICALLY with no policy at all, so the failure is
#   environmental and not this policy. The permission is there by reading, not by
#   demonstration. If push notifications stop after this ships, THIS is the first
#   thing to suspect, and reverting is one word in the header name below.
#
# WHY script-src NEEDS 'unsafe-inline'. Cloudflare injects a ~921-character
# inline script into every response at the edge -- the bot-challenge and RUM
# bootstrap. Its contents change per request, so it cannot be hashed, and
# Cloudflare gives us no nonce to reuse. 'self' alone would block Cloudflare's
# own bot protection. Verified by reading the live HTML, not assumed: our own
# build emits no inline script at all.
#
# WHY style-src NEEDS 'unsafe-inline'. 20 components set style={{...}}, which
# React renders as a style attribute. Removing them all is a real refactor and
# buys little: a style attribute cannot execute script.
#
# TWO ORIGINS THAT GREPPING THE SOURCE COULD NEVER HAVE FOUND, and which
# report-only caught on its first day live:
#
#   auth.gosalka.com  A Supabase custom domain. It is not in the code at all --
#                     638 image_url/logo_url values in the DATABASE point at it
#                     (626 menu items, 12 restaurant logos), against 242 rows
#                     still on the *.supabase.co host. Enforcing the first
#                     version of this policy would have blocked most of the food
#                     photography on a food-delivery storefront. Content in a
#                     database is part of the origin surface; the code is not the
#                     whole picture.
#
#   static.cloudflareinsights.com  Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon, injected at
#                     the edge like the challenge script but from a different
#                     host, so 'self' did not cover it.
#
# EVERY OTHER ORIGIN WAS TRACED IN THE SOURCE, none guessed:
#   www.gstatic.com          firebase-messaging-sw.js importScripts the FCM SDK
#   fonts.googleapis.com     IBM Plex Sans Arabic stylesheet, index.html
#   fonts.gstatic.com        the woff2 that stylesheet points at
#   *.supabase.co            API, storage images, and wss for realtime --
#                            useCatalogSync.ts opens a channel, so the socket
#                            scheme is required and is easy to forget
#   *.tile.openstreetmap.org leaflet map tiles on four map components
#   fcmregistrations /       token registration and Firebase installations,
#   firebaseinstallations    read from the installed SDKs
#   ingest.de.sentry.io      error reports, and the CSP reports themselves
#
# Cloudflare's own scripts are served from /cdn-cgi/ on this origin, so 'self'
# already covers them. wa.me, ipn.eg and google.com/maps are plain link targets;
# navigation is not restricted by these directives and needs no entry.
#
# The sentry_key in report-uri is the public DSN key -- it already ships inside
# the JavaScript bundle and is designed to be public.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(self)
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.gstatic.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://pqpnwxyevrsipklzmwex.supabase.co https://auth.gosalka.com https://*.tile.openstreetmap.org; connect-src 'self' https://pqpnwxyevrsipklzmwex.supabase.co wss://pqpnwxyevrsipklzmwex.supabase.co https://auth.gosalka.com wss://auth.gosalka.com https://fcmregistrations.googleapis.com https://firebaseinstallations.googleapis.com https://o4511834207682560.ingest.de.sentry.io; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; report-uri https://o4511834207682560.ingest.de.sentry.io/api/4511834268762192/security/?sentry_key=0db2410bf037e80bba50613f1685114a
